<title>MOROCCO: Morocco will not devalue dirham-finance minister.</title>
<headline>Morocco will not devalue dirham-finance minister.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's Finance Minister Mohamed Kabbaj said on Thursday Rabat had no plan to devalue its currency, the dirham, despite persistent rumours on the market.</p>
<p>The dirham has fluctuated in recent weeks to trade between 8.5 and 8.7 dirhams against the U.S. dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;These are normal fluctuations...In any case we have no plans to devalue our national currency,&quot; Kabbaj told Reuters.</p>
</text>
